<title>JAPAN: Japan MOF to auction T-bills on Wednesday.</title>
<headline>Japan MOF to auction T-bills on Wednesday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of Finance (MOF) said on Tuesday it plans to offer Treasury bills (T-bills) through a price-competitive auction on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Traders said the MOF's offer is likely to be six-month T-bills, aiming to roll over 1.4 trillion yen worth of six-month T-bills maturing on May 12.</p>
<p>They also said the MOF is expected to auction six-year Japanese government bonds (JGBs) later this week.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-33432-8570</p>
</text>
